            <ArticleTitle>An isotope-diagnostic approach to Erdheim-Chester's disease of the heart.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>274-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Erdheim-Chester's disease is a form of histiocytic granulomatosis afflicting the skeletal system and various inner organs. Apart from incidental findings of involvement of various structures and tissues, a complete diagnostic workup to evaluate afflicted bodily parts is not known. The authors we present several specific isotope-diagnostic techniques of a case to support the identification of this rare multisystem infiltrative disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
